                here, and an @tag in the body ADDS a chip rather than replacing the set.

                RETIRED, same surface: "No TO row and no note checkbox ... the address is the
                message: an @tag typed in the body is who it goes to, one signal per tag." That
                direction (2026-09-04) dropped the person you were last messaging on every new
                tag, which is the defect this row exists to remove. The 80px resting budget it
                bought is renegotiated in composer-polish.observer.test.ts against a measured
                number, not deleted. */}
            <form class="dashboard__composer" data-composer hidden>
              {/* THE REPLY BAR. Hidden until a reply is in progress, so the composer at rest is
                  the bar the mobile budget was measured against. It names the message being
                  answered and the channel that message is in, because a reply is filed in its
                  root's channel by the server and the writer cannot choose otherwise.

                  The window line is the ceiling the server clamps to: a reply may not outlive
                  the message its thread starts from, and that remaining window can be
                  milliseconds. The broadcast control is rendered only for a thread that is in
                  a channel — an unfiled thread has nowhere to broadcast to, and a control that
                  cannot do anything is a lie in a checkbox. Every sentence here is built in
                  ../../lib/thread-reply.ts. */}
              <div class="dashboard__composer-reply" data-composer-reply hidden>
                <p class="dashboard__composer-reply-target">
                  <span data-composer-reply-target-text></span>
                  <span class="dashboard__composer-reply-window" data-composer-reply-window></span>
