          2026-08-19). Same data-hooks — data-member-details gates visibility to
          owner/admin exactly as before (renderMembers sets .hidden; the harmless
          .open no-op on a non-details element is intentional). */}
      <section class="dashboard__roster-dialog-members" data-member-details hidden aria-labelledby="dashboard-roster-members-title">
        <h3 class="dashboard__roster-dialog-pending-title" id="dashboard-roster-members-title">People</h3>
        <ul class="dashboard__agent-list" data-member-list></ul>
        <p class="dashboard__form-error" data-member-error role="alert" hidden></p>
        {/* The OAuth control here is GENERATED, not written. It used to be one hand-typed
            "Sign in again with GitHub" button carrying `data-member-reauth-github`, which the
            provider sweep in components/auth/provider-buttons.observer.test.ts could not see
            AT THE TIME: its marker then looked for `data-signin*` and for `data-<provider>`, and
            neither spelling matched a name ending in the provider. That marker was widened in
            the same lane and does see it now. So the one place that
            names a provider is auth-providers.ts, and the set follows the deployment — turning
            Google on in the Supabase dashboard gives this block a Google button with no change
            here. The word "again" is not lost: the sentence above these buttons is
            FreshLoginRequired's "Sign in again, then press Remove once more." */}
        <div data-member-reauth hidden>
          <ProviderButtons buttonClass="dashboard__rail-add" />
          <button class="dashboard__rail-add" type="button" data-member-reauth-email>
            Email a fresh sign-in link
