       * enqueued for delivery (swarm.enqueue_signal_delivery reads one column), and the To:
       * row says so in words"~~ is retired 2026-09-05: every AGENT recipient is woken now, at
       * any position, and both `ask` and `note` are delivered, so the kind says nothing about
       * the wake either way. There is still no note checkbox and no hidden second wake — the
       * To: row states the whole of it, and the kind is a label on the message.
       *
       * The old refusal for ambiguous and overflowed tags is gone with the fan-out: an @tag
       * that cannot become a chip is reported ON the To: row while the reader types, and the
       * row shows the truth either way. Refusing the send as well would block a sentence that
       * merely mentions a name it does not address. */
      /* `composerRecipients` is the ONE derivation the To: row also draws, so a thread reply's
       * empty set is not a second rule written here: the row said "no recipients" and the
       * wire carries none, from the same call. */
      const recipients: BrowserSignalAudience = composerRecipients();
