         nothing else — no dropdown, and no `#` parsing of the body, because bodies contain
         `#` legitimately and a parser could not tell a heading from an address. A reply
         inherits its root's channel from the SERVER: the client may not file a reply
         somewhere its thread is not, and the edge refuses a body that names both. */
      /* A REPLY IS FILED WHERE ITS THREAD IS, and the browser does not get a say: the edge
         refuses a body that names a channel alongside a thread root, and stamps the reply with
         the root's channel itself. So the placement channel of a reply is its ROOT's, captured
         when the reply was opened, and the channel the reader happens to be looking at is not
         consulted. */
      const freshPlacementChannelId = replyRoot === null
        ? activeChannel()?.channelId ?? null
        : replyRoot.channelId;
      const freshPlacementThreadRootId = replyRoot?.id ?? null;
      /* AND WHETHER IT ALSO GOES TO THE CHANNEL. Read from the control only where the control
         is offered: `threadReplyMayBroadcast` is false for an unfiled thread, and a stale
         checked box from an earlier thread cannot leak through, because `syncComposerPlacement`
         clears it whenever the control is hidden. */
